\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The pre-registered comparison on all 3{,}080{} official Banking77 test rows. \emph  {Old} is the mean-pool head; \emph  {query} is the message-query attention head. The byte budget names the context window; \emph  {examples} is the mean number of complete retrieved examples that fit (range in the text). The old-head 5{,}120 arm is the matched-test packing of all 24 examples; its native control is the query-evaluation packing, which averages 11.9{} examples. The Jev row is the cited public run, not a rerun; its Bytes cell is the reconstructed JSON prompt size, not a model context window. Wilson intervals are 95\%; $\Delta $ and exact two-sided McNemar $p$ are against Jev's frozen per-row correctness vector. The 5{,}120 query head is a joint encoder/head fine-tune, not a length-only adaptation. Every cell is generated from \texttt  {results/jev\_query}, \texttt  {results/jev\_query\_5120} or \texttt  {results/jev\_matched}.\relax }}{5}{table.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{tab:main}{{1}{5}{The pre-registered comparison on all \PN {} official Banking77 test rows. \emph {Old} is the mean-pool head; \emph {query} is the message-query attention head. The byte budget names the context window; \emph {examples} is the mean number of complete retrieved examples that fit (range in the text). The old-head 5{,}120 arm is the matched-test packing of all 24 examples; its native control is the query-evaluation packing, which averages \POldTwoExamples {} examples. The Jev row is the cited public run, not a rerun; its Bytes cell is the reconstructed JSON prompt size, not a model context window. Wilson intervals are 95\%; $\Delta $ and exact two-sided McNemar $p$ are against Jev's frozen per-row correctness vector. The 5{,}120 query head is a joint encoder/head fine-tune, not a length-only adaptation. Every cell is generated from \texttt {results/jev\_query}, \texttt {results/jev\_query\_5120} or \texttt {results/jev\_matched}.\relax }{table.caption.10}{}}
